  sqrt(pi/2) = 1.2533141373155003
  eps at c=1:    1.0   (< sqrt(pi/2)? True)
  eps at c=1.5:  0.816497   (< sqrt(pi/2)? True)
  eps at c=2:    0.707107   (< sqrt(pi/2)? True)
  eps at c=100:  0.100000
  eps at c=1000: 0.031623
  Since eps=1/sqrt(c) is strictly decreasing in c, and c=1 gives eps=1
  < sqrt(pi/2)=1.253314, EVERY c>=1 gives eps<sqrt(pi/2) strictly.
  So the front's claimed hypothesis range '0<eps<=sqrt(pi/2)' is even
  slightly more generous than what the archive ever actually needs
  (archive needs eps<1<=sqrt(pi/2), i.e. a STRICT subset) -- the stated
  hypothesis is safe and not tight to the point of fragility for c=1.
  PASS

